-- Example: GitHub-style project configuration

namespace anthill.stage0
  fact Project(
    name: "my-github-app",
    language: "rust",
    build: "cargo",
    tools: ["cargo-build", "cargo-test", "cargo-clippy", "lint-all"])

  -- Which store holds this project's work items, and in which role (proposal 057
  -- §"Configuration & bootstrap"). A host reads this at startup and builds one of its
  -- compiled-in backends from it. Declaring none is not an error — a host may have a
  -- default — but then the configuration is invisible, which is why this example
  -- states it.
  --
  -- `mirror` because the extent is RESIDENT — workitems.anthill is loaded whole and
  -- the KB answers reads, with the store as the write-through durability leg. A
  -- backend too large or too remote to load (a SQL table, a GitHub issue list) would
  -- be `owner` instead, and this is the one line a project changes to say so.
  --
  -- `covers` names the functors THIS project defines and persists. It is not a fixed
  -- list: anthill-todo's own tracker also covers `StoreFormat`, which this example's
  -- domain does not declare — and naming an undeclared functor here is a hard
  -- `extent_bindings` refusal, not a warning, so the list must match the domain.
  fact anthill.persistence.ExtentBinding(
    store: anthill.persistence.filesystem.IndexedFileStore(
      root: ".",
      convention: anthill.persistence.filesystem.FileConvention.single_file(
        file: "workitems.anthill")),
    role: anthill.persistence.ExtentRole.mirror(),
    covers: [WorkItem, Feedback, Tag])
end
